Call read_file_content(fileId=`{{sources.ops_weekly.id}}`). The doc is large and the connector may truncate the tail — that is fine because the newest week is at the TOP. Take the first block (from the first `## <Mon DD, YYYY>` heading to the next such heading) as THIS WEEK's log, and the second block for comparison. From block 1 pull: everything under `#Team update`; the event list under `#Operation` with 報名人數; the course timeline checklist under `#Knowledge product`; any filled `Metrics` value (most are bare `#` — treat `#` as "no value"). Note which functions have NO new content vs block 2 (identical text = nothing happened, a weak signal for STALLED).

